{"id":"s2.2.12","slug":"trigonometric-formulas","title":"Trigonometric Formulas","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Knowing basic trigonometric identities is essential for simplifying complex expressions.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Fundamental Identities:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$</li><li>$1 + \\cot^2\\theta = \\csc^2\\theta$</li><li>$\\tan^2\\theta + 1 = \\sec^2\\theta$</li></ul><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Sum/Difference & Double Angle Formulas:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>$\\sin(a \\pm b) = \\sin a \\cos b \\pm \\cos a \\sin b$</li><li>$\\cos(a \\pm b) = \\cos a \\cos b \\mp \\sin a \\sin b$</li><li>$\\sin(2a) = 2\\sin a \\cos a$</li><li>$\\cos(2a) = \\cos^2a - \\sin^2a$</li></ul><p>For example, $\\sin(10°)\\cos(20°) + \\cos(10°)\\sin(20°)$ simplifies to $\\sin(10°+20°) = \\sin(30°) = 1/2$.</p>","summary":"Knowing basic trigonometric identities is essential for simplifying complex expressions.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that can be simplified using a fundamental trigonometric identity (Pythagorean, sum/difference, or double angle).","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $\\cos^2 30° + \\sin^2 30°$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\cos^2 30° - \\sin^2 30°$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $2 \\sin 15° \\cos 15°$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $2 \\sin 30° \\sin 30° - 1$.","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $1 - \\sin^2 30°$.","answer":"3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":6,"text":"If $\\cos 22° = \\sin \\theta$ and $0° < \\theta < 90°$, $\\theta =$","answer":"68","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $[2 \\sin(\\pi/3) \\cos(\\pi/3)]^2$.","answer":"3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $2 \\sin 15° \\cos 15° - 1$.","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $3 \\csc^2 45° - 3 \\cot^2 45°$.","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate $\\sin 105° \\cos 105°$.","answer":"-1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":11,"text":"If $\\sin 38° = \\cos \\theta$ and $270° < \\theta < 360°$, $\\theta =$","answer":"308","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":12,"text":"Calculate $\\sin 30° \\cos 60° - \\sin 60° \\cos 30°$.","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":13,"text":"Calculate $2 \\cos^2(\\pi/6) - 1$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":14,"text":"Calculate $(1 - \\sin 60°)(1 + \\sin 60°)$.","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":15,"text":"Calculate $2 \\sin 15° \\sin 75°$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":16,"text":"Calculate $(\\sin(\\pi/3) - \\cos(\\pi/3))(\\sin(\\pi/3) + \\cos(\\pi/3))$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":17,"text":"If $\\sin(A) = 3/5$, then $\\cos(2A) =$","answer":"7/25","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":18,"text":"Calculate $1 - 2 \\sin^2(\\pi/6)$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":19,"text":"Calculate $\\cos 75° \\sin 75°$.","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":20,"text":"Calculate $\\sin 15° \\cos 45° - \\sin 45° \\cos 15°$.","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":21,"text":"Calculate $2 - 4 \\sin^2 30°$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","trigonometry"]},{"id":22,"text":"Calculate $\\cos 95° \\cos 25° - \\sin 95° \\sin 25°$.","answer":"-1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":23,"text":"Calculate $\\sin(\\pi/6) + \\cos(\\pi/3)$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":24,"tex